From 8e99880d7f24d85dd0a131c85c9ea0a7bc981430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:39:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: curl out, every load through openweb.fetch on the
 Amiga

openweb.fetch is the only network backend: ResourceHandleAmiga.cpp loses
the curl delegate and the OB_NET switch, and every http and https load
goes through WebFetchAmiga.cpp. The cookies, redirects, the HTTP cache
hook, file: URLs and synchronous loads stay as they were.

platform/Curl.cmake is no longer included. PlatformAmiga.cmake lists the
files of the curl folder that stay, none of which calls curl: the network
types (ResourceError, ResourceResponse, AuthenticationChallenge,
ResourceRequest, ProtectionSpace, CertificateInfo), the cookie database
(CookieJarDB, CookieUtil) and the empty DNS queue. USE(CURL) stays on, as
it picks those types; their curl constructors and curl's error, HTTP
version and auth codes are left out on PLATFORM(AMIGA). CurlContext (with
patch 0010's OB_FETCH_PROXY experiment), CurlRequest,
CurlRequestScheduler, CurlFormDataStream, CurlMultipartHandle,
CurlProxySettings, CurlSSLHandle and amiga/CurlSSLHandleAmiga.cpp are no
longer built: 19 files, 4,057 lines. multipart/x-mixed-replace is not
split into parts any more, as openweb.fetch's loads never were: such a
response arrives as one body.

Every load asks for WF_DECODE, on the card and natively alike, so pages
come compressed as they did with curl: the card's host undoes gzip,
deflate and br, and the native transport does it through the datatypes
(stream.datatype with gzip.datatype and brotli.datatype; openamigaservice
#15), offering in Accept-Encoding only what it can undo. The request no
longer asks the native transport for identity.

OpenWebFetchAmiga.c needs openamigaservice's client headers: the stubs
for a build without them are gone, with obwf_available() and
obwf_net_decodes(). curl is no longer found or linked, and nghttp2 with
it.

